    "result_text": "All 13 test classes (Cp01\u2013Cp13) ran: **22 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**. The implementation is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `namesakeCount` field to the create-owner flow that records how many existing owners already shared the same first + last name (case-insensitive) at creation time.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` integer property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates into `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persistent `namesakeCount` column with getter/setter, mirroring the existing `customerCode`/`householdId` derived fields.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added `namesake_count INTEGER` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres), and appended the extra positional `NULL` to the hsqldb `data.sql` seed rows (the test DB uses column-less inserts).\n\n4. **New function `CountNamesakes.java`** \u2014 Following the existing OfficeFloor pattern (like `AssignCustomerCode`): counts `ownerRepository.findAll()` entries whose trimmed, lower-cased first+last name match the built owner, and sets it in place. It runs **after** `BuildOwner` (names exist) and **before** `SaveOwner` (so the new owner isn't counted among its own namesakes).\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Wired the new `countNamesakes` step between `build` and `assignCustomerCode`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nThe `Cp13Tests` acceptance test (two owners with the same name \u2192 second owner reads back `namesakeCount = 1`) passes, and all pre-existing tests remain green.",
